
Can be made gluten free.

Allie says tiny bit more sugar
Kim says use quick oats. (softer)


Whisk together
1 1/2 cups flour
3/4 cup brown sugar
1/2 cup white sugar
1 tsp baking soda
1 tsp cinnamon
1/2 tsp salt

Mix in..
2/3 cup olive oil
2 eggs
1 tsp vanilla

Continue to mix in..
3 cups oats
And extras - Like crushed nuts or maybe chocolate chips? Or not..

Bake
350 deg 8..10 minutes 

NOTE : I been using 10 minute bake times. That'll make them puff up. Then flatten out when cool.

NOTE : I use a 1 oz "disher" from Hamilton Beach. Also known as #30. Should give you 32 1/2 cookie balls.

NOTE : You need to mash 'em down a little so that they'll cook through. Left as balls of dough they tend to be a bit raw in the middle. To mash, wet your fingers in a finger bowl. Then the stuff won't stick to them.
